Base: cursor/c03-route-action-flow-e504 @ 91ce157df90bb2659d88842b7091851dca74e937

`RouteActionReadbackFlow.recover` is unchanged. This branch does not insert a route action.

Applied on the existing route page `App/PlayRouteMapView.swift` (`playRoute.screen`):
one quiet system-text row. The page calls `RouteActionPageRead.shownRow`, which calls
`RouteActionReadbackFlow.recover`. A different session id, member id, or action id is
not shown. The same ids keep that same row. `appear()` / `onAppear` does not call the
reader and does not write. No new localization key. No gradient, glow, or emoji icon.

`PlayRouteMapView.swift` is already in the app target. This branch does not add a
PBX file reference for it.

## Not applied

The running journey screen is `SessionPlayRuntimeView`, which only receives `AppSession`.
Passing the real `topicRouteSessionMapper.selectActionByAction` into
`PlayRouteMapView.actionRead` would require `App/AppSession.swift` or
`App/AppCompositionRoot.swift`. That mapper is not in this repo. The Xcode target
does not yet list the Core file, so compiling the page in the app target would also
require `Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`.

Do not apply the paste below from this branch. Do not edit those three files here.

```
App/AppSession.swift
App/AppCompositionRoot.swift
Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
```

